Le dimanche 18 juin 2017 16:14:31 UTC-7, Altuna Akalin a écrit :

> On Tue, Jun 13, 2017 at 8:42 AM, <youngju...@gmail.com> wrote:
> > Dear Group,
> >
> > I have following questions about removing batch effect by using methylKit (command assocComp and removeComp).
> >
> > 1. From the example (https://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/manuals/methylKit/man/methylKit.pdf), batch_id and age were used for sampleAnnotation.
> > I wonder can I use sampleAnnotation with only batch_id (or at least two parameter?).
> >
>
> yes, you can.
>
> > 2. When I conducted assocComp with 30 samples (15 control, 15 test), I got 30 PCs.
> > Is it normal to get the same number of PC as sample?
> >
> Yes, that is how PCA works. The function tests which PCs are associated with sample annotations
>
> > 3. After I conducted assocComp, I got $pcs, $vars, and $associations. I read explanation of them from here (https://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/manuals/methylKit/man/methylKit.pdf).
> > However,  But I did not understand them. More specifically, I did not understand what PC should be deleted based on what ($vars or $association? with what cut-off?).
>
> $association  matrix has the P-values that comes from a statistical test for association of PCs with sample annotations. If a PC is significantly associated with batch ids you can try to remove it, this is a crude way of dealing with batch effects.
>

