On Mon, Aug 27, 2018 at 10:30 AM <hashima...@gmail.com> wrote:
> Hi,
>
> First of all thanks for a great tool. I have some queries.
>
> I have BS (5hmc+5mc) and oxBS (5mc) data. I am trying to estimate true 5hmc and 5mc level.
> Please have a look at commands.
>
> # BS (5hmc+5mc) data
>
> WT_bs_5mc_5hmc=methRead("methyl_call/WT_bs_CpG.txt",sample.id <http://sample.id>="WT_bs_5mc_5hmc",assembly="hg19")
>
>
> # oxBS (5mc) data
>
> WT_oxbs_5mc=methRead("methyl_call/WT_oxbs_CpG.txt",sample.id <http://sample.id>="WT_oxbs_5mc",assembly="hg19")
>
>
> I just want to confirm:
>
>
> # Below command will give me true 5hmc level?
>
> WT_adjusted_true_5hmC=adjustMethylC(WT_bs_5mc_5hmc , WT_oxbs_5mc)
>
>

The first argument should be the compound measurement which includes both 5mC and 5hmC measurement. The second argument should be either true 5hmC or 5mC levels. These levels will be simply subtracted from the compound measurement.
https://github.com/al2na/methylKit/blob/master/R/adjust.methylC.R#L99

> # Below command will give me true 5mc level?
>
> WT_adjusted_true_5mC=adjustMethylC(WT_oxbs_5mc,WT_bs_5mc_5hmc)
>
>
> Also, Later I want to plot the average pattern of 5hmc and 5mc across promoter and gene-body regions. I know how to make average expression plots for ChIP/RNA seq but do you have any idea how to make them on BS and oxBS data?
>
>
> Thanks in advance, looking for a positive response.
>
> Regards
> Adnan.
>

